Create Azure AKS: 
for network set aks to ecommerce-stage-vnet-aks-subnet by select Azure CNI Node Subnet on network tab.

Managed identity: ecommerce-stage-aks-cluster-uami
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Connect to AKS:
$aksKubeconfig = Join-Path $HOME ".kube\config-ecommerce-aks"
az aks get-credentials --resource-group ecommerce-stage-rg --name ecommerce-stage-aks-cluster --overwrite-existing --file $aksKubeconfig  
$env:KUBECONFIG = $aksKubeconfig

kubectl config get-contexts
kubectl get nodes
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create namespace:
kubectl create namespace ecommerce
kubectl get namespaces
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deploy ecommerce-infrastructure:
helm install ecommerce-infrastructure ./helm-infrastructure --namespace ecommerce
helm upgrade ecommerce-infrastructure ./helm-infrastructure --namespace ecommerce
helm uninstall ecommerce-infrastructure  --namespace ecommerce 
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Enable Gateway API on the cluster:
az aks update --resource-group ecommerce-stage-rg --name ecommerce-stage-aks-cluster --enable-gateway-api --enable-app-routing-istio
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deploy ecommerce-apps:
helm upgrade --install ecommerce-apps .\helm-apps --namespace ecommerce
helm uninstall ecommerce-apps --namespace ecommerce
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Get Assigned IP for Gateway (Test if work by IP)
kubectl --kubeconfig "$HOME\.kube\config-ecommerce-aks" get gateway ecommerce-gatewaynetworking -n ecommerce -o wide
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
buy domain and connect it to the IP (test with new domain http)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Install cert-manager with Gateway API support (required for automatic HTTPS certificate issuance and renewal):
helm repo add jetstack https://charts.jetstack.io
helm repo update
helm upgrade --install cert-manager jetstack/cert-manager --namespace cert-manager --create-namespace --version v1.18.2 --reset-values --set crds.enabled=true --set config.enableGatewayAPI=true --server-side=false
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deploy ecommerce-apps again:
helm upgrade --install ecommerce-apps .\helm-apps --namespace ecommerce
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
After the Certificate reports Ready=True, use https://ecommerce.insure/
kubectl --kubeconfig "$HOME\.kube\config-ecommerce-aks" get certificate ecommerce-tls -n ecommerce
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
test with domain and https



